# Scheduling, Campaigns, Phone Queues & Attendance

Four related domains: shift scheduling (grid/templates/exceptions), call-
campaign scheduling, phone queue coverage, and the attendance points engine.
Follows
[.cursor/rules/backend-api-conventions.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/backend-api-conventions.mdc)
and, for dates, [.cursor/rules/date-handling.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/date-handling.mdc).

## Backend map (`backend/src/`)

Services are split by concern under three folders (add to the matching slice):

- `services/scheduling/` — `schedule.template.service.ts`, `schedule.shift.service.ts`
  (grid, publish/unlock), `schedule.apply.service.ts` (template → roster),
  `schedule.exception.service.ts` + `timeOff.classify.ts` / `timeOff.derive.service.ts`
  (time-off import), `schedule.listTypes.service.ts`. Shared: `schedule.types.ts`,
  `schedule.dates.ts`, `schedule.permissions.ts`.
- `services/attendance/` — `attendance.engine.ts` + `attendance.rules.ts` (points
  math — single source of truth; do not duplicate elsewhere), `attendance.config.ts` /
  `attendance.settings.ts`, `attendance.rollup.service.ts`, `attendance.analytics.service.ts`,
  `attendance.notify.ts`, and the `punchProvider.ts` / `scheduleProvider.ts` adapters.
- `services/campaigns/` — campaign library, schedules, month/day overrides, publish
  (mounted under the scheduling API prefix).
- `services/queues/` — phone queue coverage. The plan is solved on read, never
  stored, and availability comes ONLY from
  `services/attendance/scheduleProvider.ts#getScheduledShifts` — never query
  shifts or exceptions here, or queue coverage will drift from schedule coverage.
  Full reference: [docs/phone_queues.md](mdc:docs/phone_queues.md).
- Controllers: `controllers/scheduling/*` and `controllers/campaigns/*` (with a
  `respond.ts` error mapper — route errors through it, mirroring write-ups).
  `controllers/queues/*` is the exception: it is newer and uses
  `asyncHandler` + `AppError`, the canonical envelope. Do NOT add `respond.ts`
  there, and do not copy `respond.ts` into any new slice.
- Routes: `routes/scheduling.routes.ts` (`/api/scheduling`), `routes/campaign.routes.ts`
  (`/api/scheduling/campaigns`), `routes/phoneQueue.routes.ts`
  (`/api/scheduling/queues`). Both nested prefixes must stay mounted BEFORE
  `/api/scheduling` in `index.ts` or the scheduling router swallows them.
  Attendance policy CRUD + CSR reports are exposed via
  the Insights controllers (`insightsAdminAttendance.controller.ts`,
  `insightsCsr.controller.ts`), NOT a standalone attendance route.

## `getScheduledShifts` defaults to PUBLISHED — leave it alone

It takes an optional `{ publishedOnly }`. The default `true` is what stops a
stack of draft weeks marking anyone absent. Only a caller that scores nothing
(queue coverage preview) may pass `false`. Guarded by
`services/attendance/__tests__/scheduleProvider.publishedOnly.test.ts`.

## Attendance analytics = read-only

`attendance.analytics.service.ts` and the Insights attendance reads follow the
data-warehouse conventions in
[.cursor/rules/insights-data-warehouse.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/insights-data-warehouse.mdc);
do not turn analytical SQL into per-row Prisma calls.

## Frontend map

- `pages/scheduling/` — `SchedulingPage` (manager grid), `MySchedulePage`,
  `SchedulingExceptionsPage`, `CampaignSchedulePage`, `TimeOffImportReviewPage`,
  `QueueCoveragePage`.
- `components/scheduling/` — grid/cells, shift/template editors, exception editors,
  coverage bars, campaign grid components, `Queue*` coverage components. Hooks in
  `hooks/useScheduleGrid.ts` etc.; API in `services/schedulingService.ts` /
  `campaignService.ts` / `phoneQueueService.ts`.
- `CoverageBars` / `DeptCoverageRow` compute coverage on the CLIENT from
  mock-data types. Queue components deliberately do not reuse that computation —
  they render server-solved numbers and borrow only `COVERAGE_CLS` from
  `scheduleTime.ts`. Two solvers would eventually disagree.
- Admin list editors (attendance point bands / thresholds, exception & activity
  types, coverage thresholds, campaign library, phone queue library) live in
  `pages/admin/list-management/*` and are wired from `ListManagementPage.tsx`
  via `CUSTOM_EDITORS`. Obey [.cursor/rules/ui-design.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/ui-design.mdc).
